<% content_for :title, "Privacy · Nuclear Directory" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <link rel="canonical" href="<%= privacy_url %>">
  <meta name="description" content="What Nuclear Directory records: page views, searches, time on page and dead clicks, the country you're visiting from, and what you type into a correction. No accounts, no advertising trackers, one security cookie.">
<% end %>
<%= render layout: "pages/frame", locals: { current: :privacy, title: "Privacy", updated: "October 2026",
      summary: "Nuclear Directory has no accounts, no ads and no tracking cookies. We count visits to make the site better, using as little information as we can.",
      facts: [ { label: "Accounts", value: "None" }, { label: "Advertising", value: "None" },
               { label: "Cookies", value: "One, to protect forms", wide: true }, { label: "Analytics", value: "PostHog, through this site", wide: true },
               { label: "Location", value: "Country only" }, { label: "Recordings", value: "None" } ] } do %>
  <section class="nd-info__sec" aria-labelledby="collect">
    <h2 id="collect" class="nd-info__h">What we collect</h2>
    <p>We collect three things. <strong>Analytics</strong>: which pages are viewed, what is searched, how long a page stays open, and clicks on things that don't respond. <strong>Corrections</strong>: what you send us when you report a mistake. <strong>Error reports</strong>: technical details when a page breaks.</p>
    <p>We don't sell data or share it for advertising.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="nd-info__sec" aria-labelledby="counts">
    <h2 id="counts" class="nd-info__h">Analytics</h2>
    <p>We use <a class="nd-link" href="https://posthog.com/privacy" rel="noopener">PostHog</a> to understand how the site is used.</p>
    <p>No cookies, and one visit isn't linked to the next.</p>
    <p>Searches are recorded with their words, the number of results, and whether they came from a suggested search on the home page.</p>
    <p>How fast a page loads and responds, as three numbers (largest paint, layout shift and interaction delay), with no page content.</p>
    <p>When you follow a link off the site: the kind of link (a company's website or a source), the site it goes to (its domain only) and which company or plant page it was on.</p>
    <p>For a click on something that doesn't respond, we record the text that was clicked.</p>
    <p>Page addresses are recorded without their query strings.</p>
    <p>There are no session recordings.</p>
    <p><strong>Location.</strong> Our server works out which country you're in from your IP address, and adds only the country to the analytics. PostHog receives your IP address and browser with each request so it can count unique visitors without cookies. It doesn't store the IP address. Country data is <a class="nd-link" href="https://db-ip.com" rel="noopener">IP Geolocation by DB-IP</a>, used under the <a class="nd-link" href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a> license.</p>
    <p>PostHog's scripts, and the data they send, go through this site rather than straight to PostHog.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="nd-info__sec" aria-labelledby="cookie">
    <h2 id="cookie" class="nd-info__h">Cookies</h2>
    <p>We set one cookie. It protects the site's forms against forged submissions, holds no personal information, and is deleted when you close your browser.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="nd-info__sec" aria-labelledby="corrections">
    <h2 id="corrections" class="nd-info__h">Corrections</h2>
    <p>When you report a correction, we keep your message, the page it's about and, if you give one, your email address. We use your email only to reply about that correction.</p>
    <p>Your IP address isn't stored with it. To stop floods of reports, a scrambled form of it is kept for ten minutes, then deleted.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="nd-info__sec" aria-labelledby="errors">
    <h2 id="errors" class="nd-info__h">Error reports</h2>
    <p>If a page breaks, <a class="nd-link" href="https://sentry.io/privacy/" rel="noopener">Sentry</a> receives the page address and the error. It never receives cookies, form contents, query strings or anything that identifies you.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="nd-info__sec" aria-labelledby="hosting">
    <h2 id="hosting" class="nd-info__h">Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site runs on <a class="nd-link" href="https://render.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Render</a>, and fonts and scripts are served from this site. Like any host, Render keeps server logs, which include IP addresses, for a limited time to run and secure the service.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="nd-info__sec" aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact" class="nd-info__h">Questions</h2>
    <p>Email <%= mail_to DirectoryHelper::CORRECTIONS_EMAIL, nil, class: "nd-link" %>.</p>
  </section>

<% end %>
